{
  "text": "I am writing to express my extreme frustration with my recent experience at Northwind Outdoor. As a first-time buyer, I expected better service, but I have been left with a significant issue regarding my loyalty card. I accidentally lost my physical card, and I was told that replacing it costs $5.00. I find this fee completely unreasonable, especially since I have not yet had the chance to use the card for any substantial purchases. Furthermore, I was informed that the minimum purchase amount to activate or use the card is $25.00. This is a barrier that feels intentionally designed to discourage new customers. I am not asking for a free replacement, but I am requesting an exception to the $5.00 replacement fee and a waiver of the $25.00 minimum purchase requirement. I believe that as a new customer, I deserve a fairer start. I hope you can review my case and make an exception to these policies. I look forward to your prompt response."
}
